[A20] UNACCEPTED: independent manager challenge of the first #419 snapshot contract.

The author finished successfully with <agent-system-1> (3,303.58 seconds,170 turns). Its exact proposal remains unaccepted. An ERASE can change live record bytes and then terminate with an error, without a normal completion pulse. The proposed mutation and gap rules only observe successful device completion, so they miss that change.

The frozen prototype SHA256 is `394d544e75d034c0be3d4f2de961f554460ae48bf771cc78529ca1bbd736a86c`; original unit source `39342a52ba3c6de1bfe87c172eaf4507ef30eb657fcc5103d878fe481e7c8835`. Both are copied unchanged; only the external unit driver is extended. The complete production firmware, donor producer, flash, parent wiring and board are absent from this challenge. Initial and final ACKs are explicit CSR stimuli, so this establishes an invalid capture/ACK admission, not a reproduced flash promotion or board failure.

Seed a valid 28-byte binding record with final payload byte FF. Its CRC16 is independently calculated with Python `binascii.crc_hqx(header-without-CRC + payload,0xffff)`. The frame is `172202200014539803000001112233445566778899aabbccddeeffff`. Perform an ordinary successful ERASE/WRITE and a synthetic accepted ACK to establish a clean initial state.

Then request another ERASE. The external memory model commits the first 27 byte writes, returns done+error for the last byte and preserves that failed byte. Every earlier write remains committed. The final byte was already FF, so the entire record becomes FF despite the ERASE ending in error. No failing transaction is assumed to modify memory. A second case fails after six successful bytes and leaves a partial record.

| Case | Actual exit | Observation |
|---|---:|---|
| Existing 19 emitted checks across 19 contract statements | 0 | Original standing unit suite remains green |
| Error on final ERASE byte,27 successful writes | 1 | Fully erased record; dirty0,gap0,busy0; new arm valid1; ACK accepted,dirty0,backed1; two contract assertions fail |
| Error after six successful ERASE bytes | 1 | Partial record with the same false completed-capture admission; two assertions fail |
| Error on first byte,zero successful writes | 0 | Exact original record remains; unchanged-image control passes |
| ERASE completes normally | 0 | dirty1,gap1; arm invalid; ACK refused; control passes |

All memory-side byte/count assertions pass. The observed root cause agrees with the prototype: `erase_commit_w = done_r & was_erase_r`, `mut_w` includes completed WRITE/ERASE, and the backend error state emits `err_r` without `done_r`. Thus absence of a successful completion cannot prove absence of image mutation. The successful-ERASE control distinguishes missing error coverage from a generally broken capture refusal.

The model uses actual50MHz backend edges, one outstanding three-cycle byte-memory transaction, the shipping1x1 dimensions and public ports only. This challenge advances no milliseconds and makes no deadline, CPU/DDR or physical-reachability claim. It does not instantiate the ordinary donor retry path. Phase3 of #420 separately investigates that full producer/firmware boundary.

Before another contract review, account for in-flight and partial/failed mutations, including ERASE errors and abandoned logical records. Prove capture and slot promotion separately from ACK retirement; an image digest is not by itself a completed-record ownership proof. The outstanding producer change already reported before capture cannot be relabeled optional if ACK retirement excludes work not represented in the verified slot. Reassess the single gap entry after sequential failed operations on different records; one command outstanding does not by itself mean one unresolved record.

The existing #419 acceptance already requires retaining the last verified slot on failed capture/commit and preserving first-boot defaults. Committing an interrupted erased record after a timeout would change that acceptance and is not authorized by this proposal. I am retaining the existing requirement; no owner decision on that weaker alternative is needed to continue design work. Recovery and bounded reporting still require an explicit contract; a500ms debounce is not a proof of a memory-operation timeout.

Reproduction: restore the published prototype sources, generate with mkproto.py at root32f7/unchanged pins, copy `prototype/KL_nvm_backend.proto.sv` as `prototype.sv` into a fresh challenge directory, and save the complete `challenge_unit.cpp` below there. Set CHALLENGE to that directory. Build and run:

```sh
rtk proxy taskset -c 12,13 verilator --cc --exe --build -j 2 --top-module KL_nvm_backend --Mdir "$CHALLENGE/build" -Wall -Wno-fatal -GCLK_HZ_P=50000000 -GN_STREAM_IN_P=2 -GN_STREAM_OUT_P=2 -GN_SPORT_IN_P=1 -GN_SPORT_OUT_P=1 -GN_AUDIO_UNIT_P=1 -GN_CLK_DOM_P=1 -GN_NAME_P=31 -CFLAGS '-std=c++17 -O1' "$CHALLENGE/prototype.sv" "$CHALLENGE/challenge_unit.cpp" -o challenge
rtk proxy taskset -c 12,13 "$CHALLENGE/build/challenge" --variant proto
rtk proxy taskset -c 12,13 "$CHALLENGE/build/challenge" --manager-case 27
rtk proxy taskset -c 12,13 "$CHALLENGE/build/challenge" --manager-case 6
rtk proxy taskset -c 12,13 "$CHALLENGE/build/challenge" --manager-case 0
rtk proxy taskset -c 12,13 "$CHALLENGE/build/challenge" --manager-case -1
```

Build exit0 under Verilator5.050, at most2workers. The first test run's heading mistakenly printed pristine for the manager cases although the single binary linked the frozen prototype. That heading alone was corrected; the first sources/logs remain archived, and all cases were rerun with identical outcomes. No production source or prototype change was made.

<details><summary>challenge_unit.cpp (SHA256 8b6a1cd39e99c711892928c010af5f247cf2effa4e1071f51ad86d65e8f19311)</summary>

````text
// SPDX-License-Identifier: CERN-OHL-W-2.0
// Issue #419 design prototype: an RTL-only edge bench for the acknowledgement
// contract. It drives KL_nvm_backend's real device, memory and control faces
// and nothing else; no firmware, no flash and no host model take part, so the
// numbers it prints are backend clock edges and not milliseconds of anything.
//
// The same source grades the tracked module and the prototype: --variant
// selects which contract the expectations come from, so the baseline column
// in the report is measured rather than quoted.
#include "VKL_nvm_backend.h"
#include "verilated.h"

#include <cstdint>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cstdio>
#include <cstring>
#include <memory>
#include <string>
#include <vector>

namespace {

constexpr uint32_t kBase = 0x40000000;
constexpr uint32_t kAreaLen = 2652;   // the 1x1 shape's record area, bytes
constexpr uint32_t kBindOff = 122;    // record 0x20 inside the record area
constexpr unsigned kBindLen = 28;     // its framed length

std::unique_ptr<VKL_nvm_backend> dut;
std::vector<uint8_t> mem(0x10000, 0xA5);
uint64_t cycles = 0;
int failures = 0;
bool proto = false;

struct Write {
  bool busy = false;
  int delay = 0;
  uint32_t addr = 0;
  uint64_t data = 0;
  uint8_t strb = 0;
} wr;

int manager_fail_after = -1;
unsigned manager_mem_takes = 0;
unsigned manager_mem_errors = 0;
unsigned manager_mem_good = 0;
bool wr_fail_next = false;   // make the NEXT accepted memory write report err

void edge() {
  dut->clk_i = 0;
  dut->mem_wr_ready_i = !wr.busy;
  dut->mem_wr_done_i = wr.busy && wr.delay == 0;
  dut->mem_wr_err_i = dut->mem_wr_done_i && wr_fail_next;
  dut->eval();
  const bool take = dut->mem_wr_valid_o && dut->mem_wr_ready_i;
  const bool finish = dut->mem_wr_done_i;
  if (finish) {
    if (!wr_fail_next) {
      ++manager_mem_good;
      for (unsigned n = 0; n < 8; ++n)
        if (wr.strb & (1u << n))
          mem[(wr.addr - kBase + n) & 0xFFFF] = uint8_t(wr.data >> (56 - 8 * n));
    } else {
      ++manager_mem_errors;
      wr_fail_next = false;
    }
    wr.busy = false;
  } else if (wr.busy) {
    --wr.delay;
  }
  if (take) {
    if (manager_fail_after >= 0 && manager_mem_takes == unsigned(manager_fail_after)) wr_fail_next = true;
    ++manager_mem_takes;
    wr = {true, 2, dut->mem_wr_addr_o, dut->mem_wr_data_o,
          uint8_t(dut->mem_wr_strb_o)};
  }
  dut->clk_i = 1;
  dut->eval();
  ++cycles;
  dut->clk_i = 0;
  dut->eval();
}

uint32_t status() {
  const auto keep_sel = dut->csr_sel_i;
  const auto keep_we = dut->csr_we_i;
  const auto keep_addr = dut->csr_addr_i;
  dut->csr_sel_i = 1;
  dut->csr_we_i = 0;
  dut->csr_addr_i = 3;
  dut->eval();
  const uint32_t v = dut->csr_rdata_o;
  dut->csr_sel_i = keep_sel;
  dut->csr_we_i = keep_we;
  dut->csr_addr_i = keep_addr;
  dut->eval();
  return v;
}

struct Bits {
  unsigned dev_busy, cfg, backed, valid, dirty, stale, bracket;
  unsigned armed, cap_valid, gap, ack_ref, tag;
};

Bits bits() {
  const uint32_t s = status();
  return Bits{(s >> 4) & 1u,  (s >> 5) & 1u,  (s >> 6) & 1u,  (s >> 7) & 1u,
              (s >> 8) & 1u,  (s >> 9) & 1u,  (s >> 10) & 1u, (s >> 16) & 1u,
              (s >> 17) & 1u, (s >> 18) & 1u, (s >> 19) & 1u, (s >> 24) & 0xffu};
}

void csr(unsigned addr, uint32_t value) {
  dut->csr_sel_i = 1;
  dut->csr_we_i = 1;
  dut->csr_addr_i = addr;
  dut->csr_wdata_i = value;
  edge();
  dut->csr_sel_i = 0;
  dut->csr_we_i = 0;
}

// One strobe of the control word: [0] heartbeat, [1] acknowledge, [2] start,
// [3] arm (the prototype's).
void strobe(uint32_t v) { csr(4, v); }

void reset() {
  dut->rst_n = 0;
  dut->change_i = 0;
  dut->dev_req_i = dut->dev_wvalid_i = dut->dev_rready_i = 0;
  dut->mem_req_ready_i = dut->mem_rsp_valid_i = 0;
  dut->mem_rsp_last_i = 1;
  dut->mem_rsp_err_i = 0;
  dut->csr_sel_i = dut->csr_we_i = 0;
  for (int n = 0; n < 4; ++n) edge();
  dut->rst_n = 1;
  edge();
}

void configure() {
  csr(0, kBase);
  csr(1, kAreaLen);
  csr(3, 0x10u);              // firmware says: validated, VD_OK
}

// Run one device command. `ack_gap` >= 0 presents the acknowledgement strobe
// that many edges after the completion pulse; 0 is the same edge.
// Returns the edge on which dev_done_o was observed.
uint64_t command(unsigned op, unsigned rid, const std::vector<uint8_t> &frame,
                 int ack_gap = -1, bool fail_first_write = false) {
  dut->dev_req_i = 1;
  dut->dev_op_i = op;
  dut->dev_region_i = rid;
  dut->dev_offset_i = 0;
  dut->dev_len_i = (op == 2) ? 0 : uint16_t(frame.size());
  dut->dev_wvalid_i = 0;
  edge();
  if (!dut->dev_gnt_o) {
    std::printf("UNIT FAIL command rid=0x%02x op=%u: no grant\n", rid, op);
    ++failures;
    return 0;
  }
  dut->dev_req_i = 0;
  size_t sent = 0;
  bool armed_fail = fail_first_write;
  uint64_t done_edge = 0;
  for (unsigned guard = 0; guard < 20000; ++guard) {
    dut->dev_wvalid_i = (op == 1) && sent < frame.size();
    if (dut->dev_wvalid_i) dut->dev_wdata_i = frame[sent];
    dut->eval();
    if (armed_fail && dut->mem_wr_valid_o) {
      wr_fail_next = true;
      armed_fail = false;
    }
    const bool took = dut->dev_wvalid_i && dut->dev_wready_o;
    const bool done = dut->dev_done_o;
    const bool err = dut->dev_err_o;
    if (done && ack_gap == 0) strobe(2);   // acknowledge on the exact edge
    edge();
    if (took) ++sent;
    if (done || err) {
      dut->dev_wvalid_i = 0;
      done_edge = cycles;
      for (int k = 0; k < ack_gap; ++k) edge();
      if (ack_gap > 0) strobe(2);
      return done_edge;
    }
  }
  std::printf("UNIT FAIL command rid=0x%02x op=%u: never terminated\n", rid, op);
  ++failures;
  return 0;
}

std::vector<uint8_t> frame(uint8_t flags) {
  std::vector<uint8_t> f(kBindLen, 0);
  f[0] = 0x17; f[1] = 0x22; f[2] = 0x02; f[3] = 0x20;
  f[4] = 0x00; f[5] = 0x14; f[6] = 0x00; f[7] = 0x00;
  f[8] = flags;
  return f;
}

void check(const char *name, bool ok, const char *detail) {
  std::printf("UNIT %-28s %s  %s\n", name, ok ? "PASS" : "FAIL", detail);
  if (!ok) ++failures;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- scenarios

void u1_reset_and_bare_ack() {
  reset();
  configure();
  Bits b = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d, "after reset armed=%u cap_valid=%u gap=%u dirty=%u tag=0x%02x",
                b.armed, b.cap_valid, b.gap, b.dirty, b.tag);
  check("U1.reset_state", b.armed == 0 && b.cap_valid == 0 && b.gap == 0 &&
        b.dirty == 0, d);
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));          // a completed record change
  strobe(2);                              // acknowledge with no window at all
  b = bits();
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d, "no window opened, ack issued: dirty=%u ack_refused=%u",
                b.dirty, b.ack_ref);
  check("U1.ack_without_window", b.dirty == 1 && b.ack_ref == 1, d);
}

// The measured shape of the defect: how many edges of separation between a
// completed record WRITE and the acknowledgement still lose the change.
void u2_ack_gap_sweep() {
  const int gaps[] = {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 64};
  for (int g : gaps) {
    reset();
    configure();
    command(2, 0x20, {});                        // ERASE the whole record
    command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));               // WRITE the old frame
    strobe(8);                                   // warm-up window (ignored today)
    strobe(2);                                   // retire it: both reach dirty=0
    // open a window, then let a record update complete inside it
    strobe(8);                                   // ARM (a no-op on the tracked module)
    Bits before = bits();
    command(2, 0x20, {});
    command(1, 0x20, frame(0x01), g);            // WRITE, then ACK g edges later
    Bits after = bits();
    char d[256];
    std::snprintf(d, sizeof d,
        "gap=%2d edges: armed_before=%u cap_valid_before=%u -> dirty=%u ack_refused=%u",
        g, before.armed, before.cap_valid, after.dirty, after.ack_ref);
    // CONTRACT: a change that completes inside the window is never retired,
    // whatever its separation from the acknowledgement, and an
    // acknowledgement that retires nothing says so.
    check((std::string("U2.ack_gap_") + std::to_string(g)).c_str(),
          after.dirty == 1 && after.ack_ref == 1, d);
  }
}

void u3_clean_window_retires() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  Bits b0 = bits();
  strobe(8);                                     // ARM with the image quiescent
  Bits b1 = bits();
  strobe(2);                                     // ACK with nothing in between
  Bits b2 = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d,
      "dirty %u -> arm(cap_valid=%u,gap=%u) -> ack dirty=%u ack_refused=%u",
      b0.dirty, b1.cap_valid, b1.gap, b2.dirty, b2.ack_ref);
  check("U3.clean_window_retires",
        b0.dirty == 1 && b2.dirty == 0 && b2.ack_ref == 0, d);
}

void u4_duplicate_ack() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);                                     // accepted
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x01));                 // new work, dirty again
  Bits b1 = bits();
  strobe(2);                                     // a repeat with no new window
  Bits b2 = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d, "after new write dirty=%u; repeated ack dirty=%u refused=%u",
                b1.dirty, b2.dirty, b2.ack_ref);
  // CONTRACT: a repeated acknowledgement retires nothing.
  check("U4.duplicate_ack_refused",
        b1.dirty == 1 && b2.dirty == 1 && b2.ack_ref == 1, d);
}

// A window belongs to the attempt that opened it. An acknowledgement that
// follows an accepted one with no window of its own retires nothing and is
// reported as refused, even when the image has not moved at all.
void u11_second_ack_after_accepted() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);                                     // accepted
  Bits b1 = bits();
  strobe(2);                                     // a second one, image quiescent
  Bits b2 = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d, "accepted ack refused=%u; the ack after it refused=%u dirty=%u",
                b1.ack_ref, b2.ack_ref, b2.dirty);
  check("U11.window_is_per_attempt",
        b1.ack_ref == 0 && b1.dirty == 0 && b2.ack_ref == 1, d);
}

// A released attempt closes the bracket and the window at once and retires
// nothing, so a failed commit costs one debounce and not the whole deadline.
void u12_release() {
  reset();
  configure();
  strobe(1);
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(8);
  strobe(4);                                     // START: the bracket opens
  Bits b1 = bits();
  strobe(16);                                    // RELEASE
  Bits b2 = bits();
  strobe(2);                                     // a late acknowledgement
  Bits b3 = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d,
      "start bracket=%u armed=%u; release bracket=%u armed=%u dirty=%u; late ack dirty=%u",
      b1.bracket, b1.armed, b2.bracket, b2.armed, b2.dirty, b3.dirty);
  check("U12.release_closes_and_retires_nothing",
        b1.bracket == 1 && b2.bracket == 0 && b2.dirty == 1 && b3.dirty == 1, d);
}

void u5_erase_gap() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);                                     // steady state: nothing pending
  Bits b0 = bits();
  command(2, 0x20, {});                          // the producer blanks the span
  Bits b1 = bits();
  strobe(8);                                     // try to capture over the blank
  Bits b2 = bits();
  strobe(2);
  Bits b3 = bits();
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x01));                 // the producer closes the span
  Bits b4 = bits();
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);                                     // and now it converges
  Bits b5 = bits();
  char d[320];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d,
      "steady dirty=%u; after ERASE gap=%u dirty=%u; arm cap_valid=%u; ack dirty=%u; after WRITE gap=%u; final dirty=%u",
      b0.dirty, b1.gap, b1.dirty, b2.cap_valid, b3.dirty, b4.gap, b5.dirty);
  // CONTRACT: a span the producer has blanked is not a saveable state, and
  // an acknowledgement taken over one retires nothing; once the producer
  // closes it, an ordinary window converges.
  check("U5.blank_span_not_retired",
        b0.dirty == 0 && b1.dirty == 1 && b3.dirty == 1 && b3.ack_ref == 1 &&
        b5.dirty == 0 && b5.ack_ref == 0, d);
}

void u6_arm_while_busy() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);                                     // steady state
  // arm while an operation is already in flight
  dut->dev_req_i = 1;
  dut->dev_op_i = 2;
  dut->dev_region_i = 0x20;
  dut->dev_offset_i = 0;
  dut->dev_len_i = 0;
  edge();
  dut->dev_req_i = 0;
  edge();
  Bits busy = bits();
  strobe(8);                                     // the arm lands mid-operation
  Bits armed = bits();
  for (unsigned g = 0; g < 20000 && !dut->dev_done_o; ++g) edge();
  edge();
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x01));                 // the update completes
  strobe(2);
  Bits after = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d,
      "dev_busy=%u at the arm, cap_valid=%u -> after the update dirty=%u",
      busy.dev_busy, armed.cap_valid, after.dirty);
  // CONTRACT: a window opened over an operation in flight cannot retire what
  // that operation completes.
  check("U6.arm_while_busy",
        busy.dev_busy == 1 && after.dirty == 1 && after.ack_ref == 1, d);
}

void u7_gap_stuck() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});                          // blank record 0x20
  command(2, 0x21, {});                          // and 0x21, with the first open
  Bits b1 = bits();
  command(1, 0x21, frame(0x03));                 // close only the second
  Bits b2 = bits();
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);
  Bits b3 = bits();
  reset();
  configure();
  Bits b4 = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d,
      "two blanked spans gap=%u; one closed gap=%u; arm+ack dirty=%u; after reset gap=%u dirty=%u",
      b1.gap, b2.gap, b3.dirty, b4.gap, b4.dirty);
  // CONTRACT: a second blanked span while one is open is beyond the tracker,
  // and the answer is to refuse rather than to guess; reset clears it.
  check("U7.two_open_spans_fail_safe",
        b1.gap == 1 && b2.gap == 1 && b3.dirty == 1 && b3.ack_ref == 1 &&
        b4.gap == 0, d);
}

void u8_change_pin_inside_window() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);
  strobe(8);                                     // a fresh window
  dut->change_i = 1;                             // a persisted field moved
  edge();
  dut->change_i = 0;
  edge();
  strobe(2);
  Bits b = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d, "change_i inside the window -> dirty=%u ack_refused=%u",
                b.dirty, b.ack_ref);
  check("U8.change_pin_voids_window", b.dirty == 1 && b.ack_ref == 1, d);
}

// The deadline machine is untouched by the contract, and a refused
// acknowledgement must still close the commit bracket or the 8 s deadline
// would revoke a durability claim the firmware never lost.
void u9_bracket_and_deadlines() {
  reset();
  configure();
  strobe(1);                                     // heartbeat: backed
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(4);                                     // START: the bracket opens
  Bits b1 = bits();
  strobe(2);                                     // a refused ACK (no window)
  Bits b2 = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d, "start bracket=%u backed=%u; refused ack bracket=%u backed=%u",
                b1.bracket, b1.backed, b2.bracket, b2.backed);
  check("U9.refused_ack_closes_bracket",
        b1.bracket == 1 && b2.bracket == 0 && b2.backed == 1, d);
}

void u10_write_failure_keeps_gap() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);
  command(2, 0x20, {});                          // blank the span
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x01), -1, true);       // and fail its first byte
  Bits b = bits();
  strobe(8);
  Bits b2 = bits();
  char d[256];
  strobe(2);
  Bits b3 = bits();
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d,
      "after a failed WRITE gap=%u dirty=%u; arm cap_valid=%u; ack dirty=%u",
      b.gap, b.dirty, b2.cap_valid, b3.dirty);
  // CONTRACT: an ERASE whose WRITE failed leaves a blank span, and nothing
  // may retire it: the last verified slot has to stand.
  check("U10.failed_write_holds_the_gap",
        b.gap == 1 && b.dirty == 1 && b3.dirty == 1 && b3.ack_ref == 1, d);
}


// The exact-edge case in isolation: a WRITE with no preceding ERASE, so the
// window is still intact when the completion and the acknowledgement land on
// one edge. This is what separates "the change wins the dirty bit" from "the
// acknowledgement is reported as having retired it".
void u13_same_edge_alone() {
  reset();
  configure();
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x03));
  strobe(8);
  strobe(2);                                     // steady state
  strobe(8);                                     // a fresh, intact window
  Bits armed = bits();
  command(1, 0x20, frame(0x01), 0);              // WRITE, ack on the same edge
  Bits after = bits();
  char d[256];
  std::snprintf(d, sizeof d,
      "window intact at the write (cap_valid=%u) -> dirty=%u ack_refused=%u",
      armed.cap_valid, after.dirty, after.ack_ref);
  check("U13.same_edge_reported",
        after.dirty == 1 && after.ack_ref == 1, d);
}


void manager_erase_failure(int fail_after) {
  manager_fail_after = -1;
  reset(); configure(); strobe(1);
  const std::vector<uint8_t> old_frame = {0x17, 0x22, 0x02, 0x20, 0x00, 0x14, 0x53, 0x98, 0x03, 0x00, 0x00, 0x01, 0x11, 0x22, 0x33, 0x44, 0x55, 0x66, 0x77, 0x88, 0x99, 0xaa, 0xbb, 0xcc, 0xdd, 0xee, 0xff, 0xff};
  command(2, 0x20, {}); command(1, 0x20, old_frame);
  check("M.initial_bytes", std::equal(old_frame.begin(),old_frame.end(),mem.begin()+kBindOff),"independent framed record; last byte FF");
  strobe(8); strobe(2);
  check("M.initial_clean", bits().dirty==0 && bits().gap==0,"successful initial write and synthetic ACK; no flash instantiated");
  manager_mem_takes = manager_mem_errors = manager_mem_good = 0;
  manager_fail_after = fail_after;
  command(2, 0x20, {});
  manager_fail_after = -1;
  auto after_erase=bits();
  std::vector<uint8_t> expected=old_frame;
  const unsigned n = fail_after<0 ? kBindLen : unsigned(fail_after);
  std::fill(expected.begin(),expected.begin()+n,0xff);
  check("M.error_model", manager_mem_good==n && manager_mem_errors==(fail_after<0?0u:1u) && std::equal(expected.begin(),expected.end(),mem.begin()+kBindOff),"only successful memory transactions changed bytes; failing transaction preserved its byte");
  std::printf("M record_after=");for(unsigned i=0;i<kBindLen;++i)std::printf("%02x",mem[kBindOff+i]);std::printf("\n");
  strobe(8); auto armed=bits();
  strobe(2); auto acked=bits();
  std::printf("M fail_after=%d good=%u errors=%u after_erase dirty=%u gap=%u busy=%u; arm valid=%u; ack dirty=%u refused=%u backed=%u\n",fail_after,manager_mem_good,manager_mem_errors,after_erase.dirty,after_erase.gap,after_erase.dev_busy,armed.cap_valid,acked.dirty,acked.ack_ref,acked.backed);
  if(fail_after==0) {
    check("M.no_byte_change_control", armed.cap_valid==1 && acked.dirty==0,"failed first transaction leaves exact initial record unchanged");
  } else {
    check("M.changed_span_blocks_capture", armed.cap_valid==0,"interrupted ERASE changed live bytes; not a completed-record capture");
    check("M.changed_span_refuses_ack", acked.dirty==1 && acked.ack_ref==1,"an unsuccessful ERASE must not be reported as an unchanged image");
  }
}

}  // namespace

int main(int argc, char **argv) {
  Verilated::commandArgs(argc, argv);
  for (int i = 1; i < argc; ++i)
    if (std::strcmp(argv[i], "--variant") == 0 && i + 1 < argc)
      proto = std::strcmp(argv[i + 1], "proto") == 0;
  dut = std::make_unique<VKL_nvm_backend>();
  if (argc>1 && std::strcmp(argv[1],"--manager-case")==0) proto=true;
  std::printf("UNIT variant=%s\n", proto ? "proto" : "pristine");
  if (argc>1 && std::strcmp(argv[1],"--manager-case")==0) {
    manager_erase_failure(argc>2?std::stoi(argv[2]):27);
    dut->final(); dut.reset(); return failures?1:0;
  }
  u1_reset_and_bare_ack();
  u2_ack_gap_sweep();
  u3_clean_window_retires();
  u4_duplicate_ack();
  u5_erase_gap();
  u6_arm_while_busy();
  u7_gap_stuck();
  u8_change_pin_inside_window();
  u9_bracket_and_deadlines();
  u10_write_failure_keeps_gap();
  u11_second_ack_after_accepted();
  u12_release();
  u13_same_edge_alone();
  std::printf("UNIT total_failures=%d edges=%llu\n", failures,
              (unsigned long long)cycles);
  dut->final();
  dut.reset();
  return failures ? 1 : 0;
}

